module sqlite
kind library

# The whole of SQLite rides in one translation unit the toolchain compiles
# for whatever target the consumer builds; nothing is prebuilt and no make
# step exists. The vendored tree stays byte-identical to upstream — every
# build choice is a #define inside this file.
csrc all "src/beans_sqlite.c"

# SQLITE_ENABLE_MATH_FUNCTIONS uses the libm functions, which every
# supported libc serves from libc itself (glibc ≥ 2.34, musl, macOS,
# Windows) — no link row needed. A `link linux library "m"` row would
# also break `beansc run`: the interpreter dlopens manifest libraries by
# their literal name, and "m" is not a loadable soname.
